{
  "fixture_schema_version": 1,
  "description": "The Unbound-Run notice (#642): the lines that tell an operator why a Run ended without binding any issue. Only a Run that ended with one of unbound_run_outcomes, and never bound, activated or contributed to an issue, earns one. The Rust Dashboard draws these lines over a held Dashboard and adds its caller's quit hint. The Python attach client prints them after the Dashboard or line printer returns.",
  "inputs": {
    "repository": "The Run's owner/repo as gh resolves its default repository for the non-interactive Run worker: GH_REPO, else a remote gh-resolved marks, else the first remote ranked upstream, github, origin, then the rest. Null when none resolves. It is what separates a blocker inside the Pool from one outside it: skip reasons carry full owner/repo#N references, while Pool members are bare numbers. Without it no blocker can be proven inside the Pool, so every blocker is named.",
    "membership": "wrapper.afk_ready.collected replaces the Pool membership; a wrapper.pool.refreshed Membership read only adds to it, because a Membership read is authority for nothing (ADR-0042). Only the github source's candidates are called ready-for-agent issues; every other source's, or an undeclared one's, are candidates."
  },
